diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index e6e2a21a..5a296061 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Preserve built-in error constructor syntax and returning arrow frames, and use JSC syntax-selected call and property-read stack positions. Retain runtime callee parentheses and computed access, and map call, bracket, and template delimiters back to their original source. Continues the source-position fixes from [oven-sh/bun#35179](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/pull/35179), [oven-sh/bun#37396](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/pull/37396), and [oven-sh/bun#41580](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/pull/41580). Thanks @robobun!
+
 - Align WebKit and VM source-position assertions with Node's constructor locations and select these regressions for native stack-formatting changes in both fork CI lanes.
 
 - Preserve the native-context count in the fast `v8.getHeapStatistics()` adapter and avoid appending a second strict code-generation flag to inherited worker arguments.
diff --git a/docs/runtime/nodejs-compat.mdx b/docs/runtime/nodejs-compat.mdx
index 0274c5b4..e94321aa 100644
--- a/docs/runtime/nodejs-compat.mdx
+++ b/docs/runtime/nodejs-compat.mdx
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ The OpenClaw fork reports missing runtime imports without downloading npm packag
 
 `Error.prepareStackTrace` supports deletion, descriptor restoration, and accessor replacement. Nested stack formatting and throwing formatters leave later captures usable.
 
-`CallSite.getLineNumber()` and `getColumnNumber()` return one-based positions, or `null` when a frame has no source position. Stack strings include column 1 and use the same constructor positions as CallSites, pointing to the `new` keyword, including across line breaks and in `node:vm` scripts. Some expression positions still differ from Node.js because JavaScriptCore and Bun's transpiler select different syntax locations.
+`CallSite.getLineNumber()` and `getColumnNumber()` return one-based positions, or `null` when a frame has no source position. Stack strings include column 1 and use the same constructor positions as CallSites, pointing to the `new` keyword, including across line breaks and in `node:vm` scripts. The matching OpenClaw engine supplies syntax-selected positions for calls, constructors, property reads, and async continuations. Built-in error constructors retain `new`, including in returning arrows. Runtime transpilation retains callee parentheses and computed access and maps opening call, bracket, and template delimiters to the original source. File-name and eval-origin formatting still follow Bun's existing conventions.
 
 ### [`node:assert`](https://nodejs.org/api/assert.html)
 
